RTK is a separate project by the RTK Contributors, licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. This cell claims no authorship of RTK or of RTK's command
compression logic: all rewrite logic lives in the `rtk` binary.

Rewritten: the plugin's one contribution -- the pre_tool_call hook that hands the
command of a terminal call to `rtk rewrite` and, when RTK answers an accepted
rewrite (exit 0 or 3), lets the call run the rewritten command, failing open on a
missing binary, a timeout, an exit outside the protocol or any error
(__init__.py:199-222) -- and the fork's backend gate, which rewrites a command
only when the backend that RUNS it is one the profile opted in to, local by
default (__init__.py:19-27, 98-139). Both are one :TOOL hook over Nodecode's tool
dispatch, which is where an eval snippet's (sh "...") forms and a shell tool's
`command` argument can still be changed; the exit-code protocol, the 2-second
bound, the once-per-start availability probe, the warning when the binary is
missing and the per-backend opt-in are translated from the original, and
/rtk-backends reports what the hook rewrote and for which backends.

Left out: the optional desktop pane and status-bar chip (desktop/plugin.js,
desktop/), which belong to the Hermes desktop app; scripts/update.sh and the
maintainer's sync script (scripts/), since a cell installs nothing into the
user's machine and the RTK binary is the user's own; the optional
container/Containerfile, which fetches a checksum-pinned RTK release into an
image of the user's own; and the manifest and CI scaffolding that a Nodecode cell
replaces with its own .asd.

